  {
   "id": "1543258136427892968",
   "author_id": "1233523505006383184",
   "author": "Edra",
   "channel_id": "872602471690797076",
   "channel": "matsuhama-arena",
   "ts": "2026-08-29T13:56:52.074000+00:00",
   "edited": null,
   "content": "You might be seeing the multiplicative value instead of the additive value, which is how they were displayed before.\n\nImagine you have two sources of 50% fire resistance. Previously those two would add up in AUDIT to 100% (50% + 50%). That's not how the game actually calculates resists though.",
   "attachments": [],
   "embeds": [],
   "reply_to": null,
   "reply_excerpt": "",
   "url": "https://discord.com/channels/872599744793419776/872602471690797076/1543258136427892968"
  },
  {
   "id": "1543258604851691570",
   "author_id": "1233523505006383184",
   "author": "Edra",
   "channel_id": "872602471690797076",
   "channel": "matsuhama-arena",
   "ts": "2026-08-29T13:58:43.755000+00:00",
   "edited": null,
   "content": "Instead the game calculates resists as a running total. I.E\n\n1000 Fire Damage gets reduced by 50% to 500 Fire Damage.\nThat 500 Fire Damage then gets reduced by a further 50% to 250 Fire Damage.\n\nThe end result is only 75% fire resistance.",
   "attachments": [],
   "embeds": [],
   "reply_to": null,
   "reply_excerpt": "",
   "url": "https://discord.com/channels/872599744793419776/872602471690797076/1543258604851691570"
  },
  {
   "id": "1543259560490565732",
   "author_id": "1233523505006383184",
   "author": "Edra",
   "channel_id": "872602471690797076",
   "channel": "matsuhama-arena",
   "ts": "2026-08-29T14:02:31.597000+00:00",
   "edited": null,
   "content": "I believe you can AUDIT <damage type> directly to view the flat percentages for each defense and how that effects the running total.",
   "attachments": [],
   "embeds": [],
   "reply_to": null,
   "reply_excerpt": "",
   "url": "https://discord.com/channels/872599744793419776/872602471690797076/1543259560490565732"
  },
